{"@context":{"lean":"lean:","block":"block:","imports":{"@type":"@id"}},"@graph":[{"@id":"lean:module:QOU.MassTheory.JSJSingleSignedness","@type":"LeanModule","name":"QOU.MassTheory.JSJSingleSignedness","imports":["lean:module:Init","lean:module:Mathlib.Algebra.Order.BigOperators.Group.Finset","lean:module:Mathlib.Order.Monotone.Basic","lean:module:Mathlib.Algebra.Order.Group.Int"],"declarations":5,"chunks":1},{"@id":"lean:QOU.MassTheory.monotone_volume_gives_nonneg_binding","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.MassTheory.monotone_volume_gives_nonneg_binding","kind":"theorem","line":72,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/MassTheory/JSJSingleSignedness.lean#L72-L80","doc":"Monotone transport, for the opposite sign convention. Together with\n`antitone_volume_gives_nonpos_binding` this is the point: under **either**\nmonotonicity direction the JSJ contribution is single-signed, so the exclusion\ndoes not depend on which convention the framework uses — only on the map being\nmonotone at all. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.MassTheory.antitone_volume_gives_nonpos_binding","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.MassTheory.antitone_volume_gives_nonpos_binding","kind":"theorem","line":63,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/MassTheory/JSJSingleSignedness.lean#L63-L70","doc":"**The hinge, transport side.** Binding is read off the carrier volume\nthrough an *antitone* map: more volume in the bound state means more mass and\ntherefore *less* binding. So a non-negative volume addition contributes\nnon-positively to the binding — single-signed, with the sign flipped. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.MassTheory.jsj_cannot_match_negative","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.MassTheory.jsj_cannot_match_negative","kind":"theorem","line":53,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/MassTheory/JSJSingleSignedness.lean#L53-L61","doc":"**The hinge, volume side.** A term sourced from a per-isotope JSJ sum of\nnon-negative piece volumes cannot reproduce a residual that is strictly\nnegative at any isotope — hence cannot reproduce a sign-changing residual. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.MassTheory.jsj_sum_nonneg","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.MassTheory.jsj_sum_nonneg","kind":"theorem","line":47,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/MassTheory/JSJSingleSignedness.lean#L47-L51","doc":"A JSJ-sourced quantity is a finite sum of piece volumes. Hyperbolic volume\nis non-negative, so the sum is. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.MassTheory.nonneg_ne_of_neg","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.MassTheory.nonneg_ne_of_neg","kind":"theorem","line":37,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/MassTheory/JSJSingleSignedness.lean#L37-L45","doc":"A family that is non-negative everywhere cannot agree pointwise with a\nfamily that takes a strictly negative value somewhere. This is the abstract\ncontent of the KL-positivity prune and of the Faddeev–Niemi verdict alike. ","signatureChunk":0}]}